adding things to the to the difficult mode or are they taking things away from the easy mode yeah

00:19:04.740 --> 00:19:32.500
you This time we also have eight Robot Masters instead of six.

00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:37.860
And, you know, in some ways that's just like a natural thing to like make a game bigger, right?

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:40.720
Is like have more stages, have more enemies and stuff like that.

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:46.860
But in Mega Man, that's an interesting like addition because now you're talking about a lot more power ups too.

00:19:46.860 --> 00:19:57.220
And, you know, this whole rock, paper, scissors mechanic of like some, you know, really do extra damage to enemies and others actually don't hurt enemies at all.

00:19:57.360 --> 00:20:00.400
Or they're the enemy's like own power so it doesn't do anything.

00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:10.660
It's very interesting to see, you know, the game expand with the additional two levels considering that there's also like a whole second half of this game.

00:20:11.580 --> 00:20:15.220
I'm just curious, you know, first let's just talk about the Robot Masters here for a minute.

00:20:15.220 --> 00:20:18.700
Do you guys remember the Robot Masters in Mega Man 1?

00:20:18.960 --> 00:20:20.520
We really like those boss fights.

00:20:20.660 --> 00:20:23.600
They felt unique and challenging to each one.

00:20:24.140 --> 00:20:30.540
At a certain point, you even fight yourself as a cloned version of your own Mega Man where he switches to whatever power ups you are.

00:20:30.860 --> 00:20:38.120
Curious to hear if the Mega Man 2 Robot Masters are just kind of the same idea as the first one or if they improve upon them.

00:20:39.060 --> 00:20:44.140
I think that they're still just as unique.

00:20:44.140 --> 00:20:48.460
I still think that there's better and worse ones.

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:58.020
Like I made the mistake of doing Bubble Man first and had basically a useless weapon for the first couple rounds, the first couple levels.

00:20:59.300 --> 00:21:11.160
But I do think that like their design is different enough to still be compared to the original Mega Man of like, oh, these are unique boss designs, some more unique than others.

00:21:11.840 --> 00:21:14.040
I think they're on the same track.

00:21:15.220 --> 00:21:18.940
Yeah, I don't remember exactly what the – I remember some of the people.

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:23.020
I remember there was Cut Man and there was, I guess, Electricity Man or Electric Man.

00:21:23.400 --> 00:21:24.240
It's Elekman.

00:21:25.040 --> 00:21:26.840
Elekman? Yes, I think it is.

00:21:26.920 --> 00:21:29.440
Oh, they probably couldn't fit Electricity Man on there.

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:30.780
I think that's just his name.

00:21:30.900 --> 00:21:32.880
Vincent Elekman. Elekman.

00:21:32.880 --> 00:21:33.860
Yeah, is his last name, Elekman?

00:21:34.420 --> 00:21:48.920
Yeah. But it does seem like – I know people kind of like – people make fun of the Mega Man bad guys over time because there are just so many of them.

00:21:49.020 --> 00:21:50.660
And it's like when you run out of ideas.

00:21:50.920 --> 00:21:55.060
But if you really think about it, like if you're willing to get a little silly, you'll never run out of ideas.

00:21:55.060 --> 00:21:57.740
You can make anything, you know, an enemy.

00:21:57.980 --> 00:22:03.420
It's just – I think it's kind of cool the way that they keep coming up with, like, new things for the enemies to do.

00:22:03.620 --> 00:22:09.260
There was Flash Man, which I don't really fully understand why he's Flash Man and his power is to freeze time.

00:22:09.880 --> 00:22:15.480
But that's a cool, like – that's a cool different, like, gameplay mechanic.

00:22:16.160 --> 00:22:18.600
It's like Flash freezing some Oreos or something.

00:22:18.600 --> 00:22:19.700
Yeah, I guess that makes sense.

00:22:19.740 --> 00:22:27.720
Some Oreos or something. But, yeah, like that's a different gameplay mechanic that totally, like, totally changes the way you think about the enemy.

00:22:27.900 --> 00:22:29.780
And once you get the power up, the way you think about the game.

00:22:31.060 --> 00:22:38.120
And, you know, it's not just like – they're not just, like, re-skins necessarily of the original.

00:22:38.320 --> 00:22:41.120
Does anyone remember what Fire Man did in the original?

00:22:42.260 --> 00:22:45.780
I believe he – I think it was, like, made of fire.

00:22:46.220 --> 00:22:49.840
Did he, like, shoot just the – did he have the same power up as Heat Man?

00:22:49.840 --> 00:22:50.940
Or was it, like, different enough?

00:22:51.240 --> 00:22:53.360
I actually don't remember, to be honest.

00:22:53.600 --> 00:22:57.220
Like, that's one of the ones I'm wondering if it was similar, but I'd have to go back and play it.

00:22:57.360 --> 00:22:59.880
But for the most part, it does feel like these all are pretty unique.

00:23:00.160 --> 00:23:09.100
Yeah, and I think – I'm trying – the Heat Man one, you can hold down the attack button, right?

00:23:09.120 --> 00:23:11.140
And then throw, like, larger fireballs?

00:23:11.560 --> 00:23:13.120
Yeah. You couldn't do that.

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:14.660
You couldn't do that in the first game.

00:23:14.780 --> 00:23:15.600
Well, you know what?

00:23:15.600 --> 00:23:17.300
I didn't know that, actually.

00:23:17.380 --> 00:23:20.860
Okay. So I didn't use Heat Man correctly the whole time, but I still used him.

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:22.000
No, no, no, no. It's fine.

00:23:22.140 --> 00:23:27.620
Yeah, he's still – I mean, like, as long as you used him in the correct appropriate battle, you're still winning the advantage.

00:23:27.920 --> 00:23:28.860
Yeah, exactly. Yeah.

00:23:29.000 --> 00:23:31.760
But, yeah, it would have been – maybe I should have tested that out.

00:23:32.460 --> 00:23:35.980
You know, the interesting thing here is, like, you know, and we can talk about the power-ups and things,

00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:38.120
I think that's different than talking about the Robot Masters.

00:23:38.120 --> 00:23:46.840
But I actually thought this time, for the most part, the stages thematically were a lot better for the, you know, for the Robot Masters.

00:23:47.200 --> 00:23:48.980
So you have, like, Bubble Man, right?

00:23:49.100 --> 00:23:58.340
And his – first you see, like, a giant waterfall, and then you go into the water, and then, like, you're able to jump as high as you possibly want because technically that's just swimming.

00:23:58.640 --> 00:24:04.360
And I thought that was, like, really cool because then they have, you know, platforms that, like, if you hit them, it's immediate death.

00:24:04.360 --> 00:24:07.760
I think they look like sea urchins to me, but I have no idea what they're supposed to be.

00:24:07.860 --> 00:24:10.400
They're just spikes. Just spikes, sure.

00:24:11.360 --> 00:24:17.820
And then you have Quick Man, which has those, like, laser beams, which, you know, it's like a two-side thing, right?

00:24:17.940 --> 00:24:23.220
One, it's really cool for the stage, but, like, man, was that not some of the most frustrating shit in this game.

00:24:23.300 --> 00:24:24.280
Like, that is – you're right.

00:24:24.280 --> 00:24:32.740
That is the best example of, like, the thematic use of level design going with the boss and just, like, how Mega Man games are designed.

00:24:32.740 --> 00:24:43.540
But I hated that fucking level because I had to play it dozens – I think, like, maybe six or seven times before I could get past all those lasers.

00:24:43.880 --> 00:24:50.100
Yeah, I feel like you're screwed if you don't play Flash Man first to get the power up to slow down time.

00:24:50.100 --> 00:24:57.000
And I didn't do any, like, research about, like, the strategy of what level to go to first.

00:24:57.000 --> 00:24:59.920
Well, that's the correct way to do it, Sean, is to not have the strategy.

00:24:59.920 --> 00:25:01.300
You were playing the correct way.

00:25:01.300 --> 00:25:04.460
No, I think the correct way is to have, like, that metal blade.

00:25:04.900 --> 00:25:09.120
I don't know. You're not getting that, like, first – you know, you're not getting that, like, first experience.

00:25:10.340 --> 00:25:14.560
Yeah, I agree, too, where it's, like, that trial and error kind of, like, learning it.

00:25:14.880 --> 00:25:23.800
Like, I think the correct way would be to go there – go there, you know, if you end up there without, you know, the time-stopping power up or whatever power you need.

00:25:23.900 --> 00:25:26.160
And then you realize, like, okay, I'll come back to this.

00:25:26.320 --> 00:25:27.240
Then you get the time power up.

00:25:27.320 --> 00:25:29.140
Then you're like, oh, my God, this will be perfect for that level.

00:25:29.140 --> 00:25:31.500
No, I do like that, like, aha moment.

00:25:31.680 --> 00:25:36.800
Yeah, for sure. I was just making a remark about that weapon.

00:25:37.080 --> 00:25:51.180
But I think also in terms of comparison to Mega Man, not so much thematically, but the levels look just much more, like, designed to fit their boss more.

00:25:51.940 --> 00:25:59.180
Like, I remember the original Mega Man, like, just the look – the look of each level was kind of blandish.

00:26:00.300 --> 00:26:02.460
Yeah, you're just kind of, like, outside of the city, right?

00:26:02.500 --> 00:26:06.660
Like, you can always see these buildings and stuff in the background, but you're not really anywhere.

00:26:07.160 --> 00:26:09.500
Yeah, there was never anything fun in the background.

00:26:09.500 --> 00:26:17.520
Like, in this one, like, you see, like, moving gears and, like, all the – there are better, like, matte paintings, I guess, in this game.

00:26:18.100 --> 00:26:21.800
Yeah, and then there's also just, like – I don't know.

00:26:21.940 --> 00:26:30.260
Certain levels just have varying difficulties in sense of, like, you know, they always have enough health to go on, right?

00:26:30.260 --> 00:26:34.520
Like, you can kind of farm enemies in this game since they always just spawn if you move off stage.

00:26:34.520 --> 00:26:40.900
If you really need health, you should just wait it out and attack an enemy that's easy to defeat until you get the health that you need.

00:26:41.540 --> 00:26:47.980
But, you know, I'm thinking about the ones that have, like – they're not bosses themselves, but they're harder enemies.

00:26:47.980 --> 00:26:51.620
Like, in Woodman's stage, he has those giant dogs.

00:26:51.940 --> 00:26:54.040
Oh, yeah. And it's like, what is going on?

00:26:54.120 --> 00:26:57.480
Like, those dogs are just so much more powerful than any of the other enemies.

00:26:57.480 --> 00:27:03.040
It's like, I thought that was the boss the first time I ran into it, and then I had to fight it, like, two or three more times.

00:27:03.420 --> 00:27:11.980
Yeah, and it took me a few times to come up with an actual way to fight those without taking an obscene amount of health – taking an obscene amount of damage.

00:27:12.900 --> 00:27:18.040
But, yeah, those and the – I forgot the name of the guy.

00:27:18.200 --> 00:27:19.960
They're in a lot of Mega Man games.

00:27:19.980 --> 00:27:24.540
But the ones that are in, like, the mechs, like, those were kind of difficult, too.

00:27:24.540 --> 00:27:38.860
And I do – like, it's glad that these games have a wider variety of enemies and not just, like, a variety of, like, one sprite enemies like we've seen in a lot of other games.

00:27:39.000 --> 00:27:47.280
Like, there are some that could be seen as mini bosses, some that can be seen as just, like, just a common.

00:27:47.280 --> 00:27:55.060
But at least, like, a variety in presentation for enemies, too, is pretty cool to see.

00:27:55.380 --> 00:27:57.040
Yeah, that is a good point, Sean.

00:27:57.100 --> 00:28:00.260
You're not just dealing with Goombas and Goombas with projectiles.

00:28:00.380 --> 00:28:05.640
Yeah. You know, like, the mech guy you're talking about, apparently his name is Sniper Armor.

00:28:05.860 --> 00:28:12.640
But, like, you can defeat the mech, and then he actually jumps out of the exploding mech, and then you have to fight him.

00:28:13.060 --> 00:28:15.440
Yeah. You know, like, that's a fun thing.

00:28:15.700 --> 00:28:25.760
There's that other guy who's in the Metal Man stage where he's, like, on a gear, and you shoot the gear that he's, like, rolling on first, and then you have to kill him.

00:28:25.920 --> 00:28:29.740
Like, he's not dangerous or anything, but you have to make sure that you take out both of them.

00:28:29.800 --> 00:28:31.660
They're not just, like – they're not together.

00:28:31.820 --> 00:28:32.860
They're not a concurrent twin.

00:28:32.880 --> 00:28:34.900
Yeah, or you kill him, and you have to dodge the gear still.

00:28:35.320 --> 00:28:36.420
Yeah, yeah, exactly.

00:28:36.740 --> 00:28:43.340
Or, you know, in Airman stage, the fan thing, the guy who has, like, a fan for a body.

00:28:44.340 --> 00:28:51.700
Not an annoying enemy, doesn't really do anything to you, but if you're just kind of rushing through the level and you don't notice him, he might blow you off the platform.

00:28:52.660 --> 00:28:58.240
Yeah, it was cool the way that they, like, interact with you other than just attacking you, or they interact with each other, you know?

00:28:58.360 --> 00:29:02.740
Like, it felt more – I don't know, more like a lived-in, like, real place.

00:29:04.140 --> 00:29:08.080
Whenever there's giant fan-belly people, it makes me think of real places.

00:29:08.960 --> 00:29:12.420
Yeah. Mega Man definitely is designed for people.

00:29:13.080 --> 00:29:30.600
Yeah. Let's talk about those platforming additions, right?

00:29:30.720 --> 00:29:37.200
Because other than the main power-ups you get, there are three, you know, I'm going to call them platforming power-ups.

00:29:37.740 --> 00:29:39.220
You mean item one, two, and three?

00:29:39.780 --> 00:29:41.740
Is that really what they're called in the game?

00:29:41.820 --> 00:29:42.720
I can't remember. Yes.

00:29:42.720 --> 00:29:44.220
But that's funny.

00:29:44.860 --> 00:29:47.220
We'll call them platforming power-ups.

00:29:47.220 --> 00:29:50.440
And one is, like, a levitating platform.

00:29:50.600 --> 00:29:54.680
The other one is, like, a jet that you get on and rides you across a stage.

00:29:54.800 --> 00:30:03.300
And then the third one actually can climb walls, although you kind of have to figure that one out a little bit by yourself because – or look at the manual, I suppose.

00:30:03.480 --> 00:30:09.540
Because when you first deploy it, it looks like it's just designed to, like, hop through the stage.

00:30:10.360 --> 00:30:13.500
Oh, yeah. You just sort of throw it.

00:30:13.940 --> 00:30:21.380
Let me hear, Joe, what did you think of the addition of platforming power-ups instead of just, you know, weapons?

00:30:21.740 --> 00:30:22.760
Well, I think it was great.

00:30:22.860 --> 00:30:29.660
I think that this is their solution to the problem we had with the first game because wasn't it a platformy thing that you needed?

00:30:29.940 --> 00:30:33.440
Like a platform gun that you needed or something that would get you up higher?

00:30:33.620 --> 00:30:34.800
The magnet gun. The magnet gun, yeah.

00:30:34.800 --> 00:30:43.480
That's right. And, like, that – you needed that to progress, whereas this is, like, a similar thing where it's, like, interacting with the environment in a way that will get you through it.

00:30:44.920 --> 00:30:53.360
But I'm assuming it gives you each of these items, like, every time you beat, you know, two or three stages, you get a new – you get item one.

00:30:53.520 --> 00:30:55.240
And then after three more stages, you get item two.

00:30:55.340 --> 00:30:56.940
And after the next two, you get item three or whatever.

00:30:57.120 --> 00:31:01.860
So that way, when you get to the stage where you need those things, you have to already have them.

00:31:01.940 --> 00:31:04.280
And it's all about just thinking about how to use them.

00:31:04.780 --> 00:31:07.400
I will say that I did never use item three.

00:31:07.940 --> 00:31:09.280
I never had a reason to.

00:31:09.400 --> 00:31:10.360
I never found a reason to.

00:31:11.300 --> 00:31:12.580
So that felt a little weird.

00:31:12.820 --> 00:31:14.580
I think those are more for, like, shortcuts.

00:31:15.260 --> 00:31:21.260
Yeah, probably. Yeah, if anything, item two is the one, you know, the jet.

00:31:21.400 --> 00:31:23.960
That's the guy. But, Sean, I'd love to hear your thoughts.

00:31:23.960 --> 00:31:35.540
I guess mine's not really a complaint in more – more so I just wish that they had taken the opportunity to, like, not separate them out.

00:31:35.760 --> 00:31:41.440
Like, oh, these are the items you use to, like, do damage to enemies.

00:31:41.440 --> 00:31:46.120
And these are the items you use to move around the world.

00:31:46.140 --> 00:31:50.360
I would have thought it would be cool if they combined those.

00:31:50.660 --> 00:31:56.460
Like, I always like games that have abilities that have more than one use.

00:31:58.080 --> 00:32:03.280
So sort of separating them out felt a little basic to me.

00:32:03.460 --> 00:32:09.080
But I did appreciate, like, that at least they were thinking about more than just how to inflict damage.

00:32:10.440 --> 00:32:12.980
Just could have been a bit more creative about it.

00:32:13.420 --> 00:32:22.740
That's a great point, though, Sean, because if you think about it, right, like the jet, the one that we all think is the most useful, that one you get for defeating Airman, right?

00:32:22.900 --> 00:32:32.200
So what's stopping you from instead making the tornado-like air projectile something that you can hop on and ride as well?

00:32:32.420 --> 00:32:36.200
You know, so this way it's like it does damage to enemies, but you can also ride through it.

00:32:36.280 --> 00:32:40.760
But if you come into contact with an enemy on it, then it, you know, disappears.

00:32:40.760 --> 00:32:43.160
Like, you can't just continue to roll steam through it.

00:32:43.400 --> 00:32:46.920
It's like there's a – it does have two functions without being two op.

00:32:47.560 --> 00:32:57.820
Yeah. You know, that does make me think, though, like, what is the point of hiding these behind particular boss battles when you're already receiving a power-up?

00:32:59.080 --> 00:33:04.520
Controversially here, but I kind of feel like you could have just started with these three, and it could have just been included in the story that Dr.

00:33:04.620 --> 00:33:05.700
Light's like, you know,

00:33:05.700 --> 00:33:11.940
Oh, shit, Wily's back, and this time he made his own robots, so I got to upgrade Mega Man and give him these three power-ups.

00:33:12.040 --> 00:33:14.940
He should just start the game with them, so this way there's no, like –

00:33:14.940 --> 00:33:24.320
I still think that they should be sprinkled in just so that you're not overwhelming the player with all these new options.

00:33:24.320 --> 00:33:38.660
Yeah. Um, but I don't think they should be locked behind specific bosses, but, like, just whatever – after whatever the first two bosses, you get number one, and then after the next two, number two, and so on and so forth.

00:33:38.920 --> 00:33:50.380
Just so that, like, you have more options the more you go through the game, but it doesn't really have these weird arbitrary connections to any one boss.

00:33:50.840 --> 00:33:58.800
Yeah, it also gives you the opportunity – it gives the developers the opportunity to put things into their levels that the player will say, like, Oh, how can I possibly get to that?

00:33:58.940 --> 00:34:05.660
And then later on when they get the power-up, like, next time they're playing the game, next time they're playing that level, they can be like, Oh, like, I get that power-up first.

00:34:05.940 --> 00:34:10.740
I can come back here and ride that up to the – you know, it leaves room for little secrets and stuff.

00:34:10.860 --> 00:34:17.700
Yeah. Um, but also to what, you know, to what you guys were saying about, like, separating them out a little bit, I think that even if they had –

00:34:17.700 --> 00:34:29.860
I did also think it was weird that they – that it, like, this platform, whether you're talking about the vertical platform and the horizontal platform, they are, like – they replace your gun.

00:34:30.020 --> 00:34:36.400
So, like, while it's going, while you're on it, after you've shot it, even while you're riding it, you can't use another weapon.

00:34:36.980 --> 00:34:50.580
So, like, I feel like it would have been interesting to kind of have those things separate so it's, like, you can use your platform and then pick your weapon and then, like, ride up and shoot at enemies from the platform and it could, like, add this whole other level of, like, the way you approach combat, too, not just navigation.

00:34:50.980 --> 00:35:03.660
Yeah. I think that that would be – that would be the easy solve, Joe, right, is, like, making sure that it's just limited to – if you're using an item or a weapon, you can only use – you know, like, say you're using weapon.

00:35:03.660 --> 00:35:06.780
You can use an item or, say you're using item, you can use a weapon.

00:35:06.840 --> 00:35:18.340
But maybe they just weren't able to get around that and my worry there would be, like, then what's just stopping you from spamming item, item, item to, you know, to, like, almost break the platforming parts of this game.

00:35:18.340 --> 00:35:20.680
You can only have – because you have ammo for the items, right?

00:35:21.320 --> 00:35:39.580
I mean – No, no, I know, but I'm saying, like, you know, the levels are only so long or so tall anyway, but, like, theoretically there are certain platforming challenges that if you can use item two as the jet and then spawn item one the platform, you're kind of always guaranteed both a horizontal and vertical advantage.

00:35:39.580 --> 00:35:40.380
Well, that's not what I mean.

00:35:40.420 --> 00:35:48.540
I mean if the jet, the platform, and the wall climbing thing are all items and then the weapons are weapons.

00:35:48.620 --> 00:35:52.000
You can be on the jet and you can still fire your gun, you know?

00:35:52.060 --> 00:35:53.520
Right, and I agree with you there.

00:35:53.620 --> 00:35:56.280
I'm saying, like, I just don't think they could have programmed them to –

00:35:56.280 --> 00:35:58.100
Maybe. Because they're all on the same menu screen.

00:35:58.300 --> 00:36:10.040
Right. You know, I feel like it'd be impossible to be like, no, these ones can only be shot at the same time given that, you know, that you need to go into that menu and change to be in that form.

00:36:10.220 --> 00:36:16.520
But do we know – I mean is it – on the NES, is it asking too much?

00:36:16.520 --> 00:36:17.480
I really don't know.

00:36:17.720 --> 00:36:23.580
To say, like, okay, well maybe just hit select and you can cycle through your platforms and then hit start and you can cycle through your things.

00:36:23.580 --> 00:36:25.960
I don't think it was a technical impossibility.

00:36:26.240 --> 00:36:30.880
I think it's a combination of they didn't think of it and game balance.

00:36:31.100 --> 00:36:42.060
Like, it's not – it's definitely not technically impossible to do both because there are moving platforms normally in this game.

00:36:42.360 --> 00:36:50.740
But regardless, I do think that it would – if they balanced the game correctly, it could have added another layer.

00:36:51.480 --> 00:36:55.060
But it's not the end of the world that they didn't, I guess.

00:36:55.500 --> 00:36:59.980
Yeah, I agree. It feels like it is a step on – it's like, okay, they improved from the first game.

00:36:59.980 --> 00:37:01.620
Maybe in the next game they'll improve that.

00:37:01.700 --> 00:37:07.340
And like, okay, now how can we – you know, it does feel like it's like an iteration on something that will probably get better in later Mega Man games.

00:37:08.140 --> 00:37:16.360
Yeah, because, you know, like, select as a – as like a cycle through your power-ups or even just your platforming power-ups is a great idea, Joe.

00:37:16.520 --> 00:37:26.060
And I'm kind of surprised that we're still, like, cycling through a long menu, you know, especially once you get to the Wiley stages that, like, you have every single power-up.

00:37:26.060 --> 00:37:31.000
You have all these different things, and they just have, like, one-letter attributes for what they are.

00:37:31.060 --> 00:37:34.140
And it's not that hard to remember that B is for bubble or anything.

00:37:34.500 --> 00:37:47.160
But it's just, like – it's a little more convoluted, or they could have made it maybe a little dressier where, like, it actually takes you into a screen where you would see, you know, like, a description of what it does or something like that.

00:37:47.160 --> 00:37:49.100
Or see Mega Man's colors change or something.

00:37:49.140 --> 00:37:51.660
I don't know, something cool. But that's just a nitpick there.

00:37:51.660 --> 00:37:58.800
I feel like the select through the thing is a much more elegant way of dealing with, like, changing in real time.

00:37:59.040 --> 00:38:07.380
And the menu screen is, like, a pause element and changing your item kind of prevents you from doing it, like, often enough.

00:38:07.600 --> 00:38:13.080
Like, I feel like if I was just able to cycle through the weapons while I was playing, I might use more.

00:38:13.080 --> 00:38:18.680
But because I have to make the active choice to pause in the menu, select which item I want to use,

00:38:18.680 --> 00:38:22.020
a lot of times I found myself just using the regular charge beam.

00:38:22.340 --> 00:38:29.020
Exactly. I mean, I remember back in – I don't remember how long ago, but the first Mega Man game I played was Mega Man 8.

00:38:30.220 --> 00:38:39.840
And I think it was just, like, the shoulder button switched between your powers, and you would see his colors change in real time and the little indicator change.

00:38:39.840 --> 00:38:49.020
So, I mean, just by virtue of having all these things to play with, I would just, like, get crazy and, oh, I want to play with this thing now.

00:38:49.120 --> 00:38:57.980
Like, whereas you don't really have that level of creativity in this one because it's kind of a drag to go to the menu and come back.

00:38:58.280 --> 00:39:06.760
In this one, you're more like, well, I know that this is the correct strategy, or I have formulated that this is the correct strategy, so I'm going to change now.

00:39:08.180 --> 00:39:12.420
So, it's just, like, it sort of – it encourages different kinds of play.

00:39:25.620 --> 00:39:35.280
I think it's time to talk about the most interesting part of any Mega Man game, and that is the power-ups that you get rewarded from the Robot Masters and stuff like that.

00:39:35.280 --> 00:39:44.000
But in this game, you have the air shooter, the crash bomber, the time stomper, the quick boomerang, the metal blade, the bubble lead, apparently.

00:39:44.000 --> 00:39:44.980
I just thought it was a bubble.

00:39:45.100 --> 00:39:46.200
I don't know what lead means.

00:39:46.660 --> 00:39:49.360
Bubble lead? It was lead. But would it be a lead?

00:39:49.500 --> 00:39:50.400
I mean, I don't know what that means either.

00:39:50.400 --> 00:39:51.580
It falls to the ground, right?

00:39:52.080 --> 00:39:54.860
Yeah, it falls to the ground, but then it's just like a bubble, right?

00:39:54.860 --> 00:39:56.940
It doesn't, like – It's a metal bubble.

00:39:58.420 --> 00:40:03.700
There you go. I don't know. Okay, it's the bubble lead, and it's the atomic fire, and then finally the leaf shield.

00:40:04.380 --> 00:40:11.580
You know, say what you will about, you know, power-ups and shmups and stuff like that.

00:40:11.580 --> 00:40:28.000
But power-ups in Mega Man and specifically in this Mega Man game, you know, it's like they're a totally different type of beast because, like, you know, you really do feel like each one makes you a little stronger in a totally different way.

00:40:28.200 --> 00:40:34.880
Like, I'm kind of confused about which one I should go after first considering the usefulness of all of them, right?

00:40:35.400 --> 00:40:36.540
No, it's the metal one.

00:40:37.440 --> 00:40:39.180
Why do you like the metal one so much?

00:40:39.180 --> 00:40:41.140
I feel like that one actually sucks, though, right?

00:40:41.240 --> 00:40:42.600
The metal one is, I think, strong.

00:40:42.600 --> 00:40:45.540
I know I just said they're all great, but, like, it doesn't take down metal enemies.

00:40:45.820 --> 00:40:55.940
Yeah, but it takes down almost every enemy, and you have a ton of ammo with it, and you get enough ammo pickups that it's basically unlimited.

00:40:57.080 --> 00:40:59.280
And it's like the weakness of three bosses.

00:40:59.920 --> 00:41:10.520
Like, I went bubble first, and maybe just because I went in a different order than you, Sean, but I found it very useful on, like, the next, at least the very next level where there were a lot of enemies that I would just...

00:41:10.520 --> 00:41:13.240
Half the stuff I used the bubble on, it just bounced right off.

00:41:13.240 --> 00:41:14.600
I mean, same after that.

00:41:14.780 --> 00:41:16.220
But, like, yeah, I feel like there were...

00:41:16.220 --> 00:41:25.140
So, like, yeah, it does have the element of, like, rock, paper, scissors, where it's like, does this beat that kind of thing?

00:41:25.260 --> 00:41:30.120
But it also, to Mike's point, like, gives you other...

00:41:30.640 --> 00:41:36.800
Like, it does more than just, like, hey, oh, bubble-type damage does good against, you know, fire-type enemies.

00:41:37.240 --> 00:41:52.820
It also, like, each, you know, bubble damage, you know, bubbles go along the ground and hit enemies that are along the ground, and you got the leaf shield, which is good against certain enemies, but also puts a shield around you, which I found really useful and interesting, and made me think about levels in different ways.

00:41:53.040 --> 00:41:59.240
Like, it's cool that it's not just, like, type advantages, but there's also, like, a function to each of these.

00:41:59.320 --> 00:42:01.060
Yeah. No, I do like that.

00:42:01.060 --> 00:42:20.220
Yeah, the leaf shield, specifically, too, of the having a way to, like, you know, not have invulnerability, but to have a, like, a little shield for a second, and then choosing the direction that that shield, like, flies off in is also a cool thing instead of just...

00:42:20.220 --> 00:42:28.020
Yeah, no, I think this is the best designed one in terms of it having more than one use as, like, a defensive and an offensive weapon.

00:42:29.680 --> 00:42:33.380
It has very different mechanics than most of them.

00:42:34.200 --> 00:42:37.800
Yeah, the leaf shield is my favorite.

00:42:38.760 --> 00:42:40.220
Yeah, it's up there for me, too.

00:42:40.260 --> 00:42:41.100
It might be mine as well.

00:42:41.820 --> 00:42:46.440
The one thing I didn't like about this bubble, that I think Joe just said bubble eight times.

00:42:47.260 --> 00:42:55.380
Bubble bubble. The one thing I didn't like about it is that when you get to, like, one of the later stages, I think it's, like, widely stage four or something like that,

00:42:55.380 --> 00:43:02.160
when you get to that, you have to use the bubble to detect where, like, the holes in the ground are, right?

00:43:02.240 --> 00:43:03.080
Like, that's the idea.

00:43:03.220 --> 00:43:09.480
It's, like, because the bubble goes right to the ground and then flies across the stage, it will fall through these pits, and then you'll know where the pits are.

00:43:10.080 --> 00:43:15.880
Why wouldn't they just, like, gray them out a little bit or, like, you know, make you pay attention a little extra?

00:43:16.380 --> 00:43:22.860
Like, that to me is, you know, there's no consequence to the bubble design of the weapon or anything like that.

00:43:22.960 --> 00:43:26.460
Yeah, it's kind of a weak way to give a weapon another use.

00:43:26.580 --> 00:43:27.640
Right, exactly.

00:43:28.060 --> 00:43:37.360
That's more what I mean is, like, yeah, it's still a cool weapon and everything like that, but now it's, like, a tedious requirement instead of, like, an actual fun part of platforming.

00:43:37.360 --> 00:43:46.040
I don't know. I sort of, I sort of, because when I first got to that part where you're falling through, I was, like, okay, this is one of those major flaws with this game where it's, like, okay, this is just kind of cheap.

00:43:46.260 --> 00:43:52.220
There's no way, there's just, like, it's just a way to make it harder without you knowing and you might just die until you learn the level.

00:43:52.520 --> 00:44:03.560
But then, like, when I thought about it, when I, like, realized you can use the bubble, I actually thought that was kind of a cool mechanic, too, because it really, it makes you think about the levels and the power-ups you have and, like, what do you have at your disposal.

00:44:03.560 --> 00:44:08.900
Like, the whole game has these little puzzly elements, like, a little bit where it's, like, well, what can I use here?

00:44:09.080 --> 00:44:10.900
Like, why would this work on this enemy?

00:44:11.060 --> 00:44:14.960
But then it's also just, like, well, how can I learn this stage?

00:44:15.160 --> 00:44:17.280
I guess I'm thinking about it in a different way.

00:44:17.600 --> 00:44:19.680
Like, that would be a cool moment.

00:44:20.300 --> 00:44:26.400
I guess I, like, watched enough things to know that, like, oh, this is how you know where the holes are.

00:44:26.400 --> 00:44:38.360
But if I'm just, like, trying to brute force this and then I realize, oh, I could just use the bubbles and this is, like, so much easier, I guess then I would feel a lot better about it.

00:44:39.220 --> 00:44:46.940
But, yeah, it's satisfying, at least from my perspective, having not known anything about, like, I mean, other than it's a Mega Man game, about, like, what these power-ups do.

00:44:47.080 --> 00:44:53.020
It was satisfying to, like, stop for a second and be like, okay, how can I, like, what has the game given me at my disposal?

00:44:53.220 --> 00:44:55.700
And then, like, remember, okay, the bubbles hug the ground, maybe it'll fall through.

00:44:55.880 --> 00:45:01.800
And, you know, that was just a cool, you know, it didn't, like, they could have done more with it.

00:45:01.880 --> 00:45:04.080
It was just, like, two screens that, like, had that ability.

00:45:04.180 --> 00:45:06.140
But it was a cool little puzzle to solve.

00:45:07.120 --> 00:45:11.420
Yeah, or you could just use the jet and fly across those platforms.

00:45:12.300 --> 00:45:13.320
Not all of them, though.

00:45:13.520 --> 00:45:17.480
Not all of them. Because some of them you couldn't, some of them were too narrow, you couldn't fire the jet out.

00:45:17.700 --> 00:45:23.960
I tried it. Oh. Or if you fired it out, you couldn't jump onto it because you were, like, you were, like, wedged in between a ceiling and a floor.

00:45:24.980 --> 00:45:29.160
See, but now, like, even though I just found this out, like, you're revealing it to me, I'm disappointed.

00:45:29.460 --> 00:45:34.860
Like, it should be designed in a way where you can use, you know, like, Mega Man has such a huge arsenal.

00:45:34.860 --> 00:45:39.760
You should be able to use a multiple different combo of things to get across these stages.

00:45:40.080 --> 00:45:42.700
Now to find out, like, oh, well, your jet's not useful there.

00:45:42.700 --> 00:45:44.660
It's like, well, that's how I want to solve the puzzle.

00:45:44.680 --> 00:45:45.640
I guess you could also just guess.

00:45:46.180 --> 00:45:50.040
But it's useful in, it's useful earlier in some of those parts.

00:45:50.040 --> 00:45:52.560
But then when you get to the top, there's one where now you can't use it anymore.

00:45:52.760 --> 00:45:55.540
So if you were using it, you'd have to think, like, okay, well, now what do I do?

00:45:55.600 --> 00:45:57.020
You know, it's like, I solved it that way.

00:45:57.140 --> 00:45:59.760
They're like, now what do I do on this one where I won't be able to use it?

00:46:00.020 --> 00:46:01.140
Well, now I love it again.

00:46:02.500 --> 00:46:03.840
But then, no, I'm just kidding.

00:46:05.600 --> 00:46:07.480
Right, right, right. Now convince me I hate it.

00:46:07.640 --> 00:46:11.300
Yeah. Anything else to say about these power-ups?

00:46:11.580 --> 00:46:16.040
You know, obviously, like, we talked so much in the first episode about the rock, paper, scissors mechanic.

00:46:16.040 --> 00:46:17.680
I don't think we need to go over that again.

00:46:17.680 --> 00:46:30.840
But I will just say, like, the overall, like, amount of use these power-ups get from someone like me who doesn't think about the strategic matchup of enemy-to-enemy basis.

00:46:30.840 --> 00:46:33.540
I still feel like I'm underutilizing these power-ups.

00:46:33.700 --> 00:46:38.280
Well, that's also because, like, there are some that are just not all that useful.

00:46:38.920 --> 00:46:40.140
Right, right. That's what I'm saying.

00:46:40.140 --> 00:46:41.260
I'm going to blame the game here.

00:46:41.260 --> 00:46:42.100
I'm not blaming myself.

00:46:42.100 --> 00:46:43.180
I'm not a bad player.

00:46:43.340 --> 00:46:45.420
It's the game that's not encouraging me to be more creative.

00:46:45.420 --> 00:46:46.400
It's the game that's wrong.

00:46:46.400 --> 00:46:53.400
I would say that, like, the boomerang, kind of dumb.

00:46:54.900 --> 00:47:05.260
The explosive that you plant, I think it's got, like, four or five, like, environmental uses in the game.

00:47:05.820 --> 00:47:09.320
And it's kind of unwieldy otherwise.

00:47:10.040 --> 00:47:13.880
And there's that one boss that you have to have a full stack.

00:47:13.900 --> 00:47:23.100
Exactly. I have never gotten to that point, but I've watched enough about this game to know, like, that that's sort of the nightmare level.

00:47:25.900 --> 00:47:28.760
And, yeah, some of them are just too situational.

00:47:29.040 --> 00:47:32.560
Like, the whirlwind is, like, only good in one direction.

00:47:33.000 --> 00:47:35.900
Like, they gave, like, again, the metal thing.

00:47:36.080 --> 00:47:38.960
They gave you the opportunity to shoot in eight directions with that.

00:47:39.140 --> 00:47:41.040
And the whirlwind is only good in one.

00:47:41.340 --> 00:47:43.280
So why not just use the metal thing?

00:47:43.280 --> 00:47:52.420
Unless you really just want that color that it adds that you're using a different weapon.

00:47:53.780 --> 00:47:55.220
So I don't know.

00:47:55.340 --> 00:48:03.580
They could have done a lot better at making them all either just as useful or at least just as fun to use.

00:48:04.900 --> 00:48:07.540
Yeah. Some of them had that.

00:48:07.620 --> 00:48:08.540
I feel like most of them.

00:48:08.640 --> 00:48:12.220
I was pretty impressed that most of them I felt like I had reasons to use a lot.

00:48:12.380 --> 00:48:16.880
But, yeah, the wind one or the air one, not super useful.

00:48:17.020 --> 00:48:24.160
There were one or two times where it was nice to get that, like, weird, like, exponential curve angle of it.

00:48:24.160 --> 00:48:26.740
But, yeah, and widespread.

00:48:27.180 --> 00:48:35.440
But then, yeah, the one that bothered me the most, I think, was the, I'm forgetting all the real names of these, but the bomb that, like, latched onto things.

00:48:35.780 --> 00:48:47.740
Because of what you guys were saying where it's, like, I think it was cool to use it in that battle where you have to, like, blow up all those little turrets on the wall or whatever those little bubble things are.

00:48:48.260 --> 00:48:49.320
That was neat.

00:48:49.400 --> 00:48:52.940
But it felt so artificial of a reason to ever use that.

00:48:52.940 --> 00:48:56.500
Like, it's the only time you ever need to use it because they just designed a quick boss battle where you need it.

00:48:56.920 --> 00:49:01.260
Where there was no time in the actual game where I was like, oh, I could really bomb something right now.

00:49:01.440 --> 00:49:06.860
You know, except there, you know, once in a while there's some walls that you can bomb to get through to get to, like, some secret areas.

00:49:06.880 --> 00:49:12.780
Not often enough to make it feel like it's very organically implemented into the game.

00:49:13.120 --> 00:49:18.000
Exactly. And why does bombing make that turret thing just, like, disappear immediately?

00:49:18.320 --> 00:49:20.300
Like, you don't even have to wait for the bomb to go off.

00:49:20.380 --> 00:49:22.180
It just makes contact with it.

00:49:23.100 --> 00:49:29.860
I thought at first because, like, the shape of the bomb that you placed, it looks like it was just, like, covering up the, you know, like, the...

00:49:31.140 --> 00:49:32.280
Wherever the... The turret.

00:49:32.620 --> 00:49:35.300
Yeah, the turret or whatever the lasers are coming out of.

00:49:35.540 --> 00:49:37.140
But, yeah. And then it blows up.

00:49:37.400 --> 00:49:46.340
But, yeah, I wonder if that was just, I don't know, some weird limitation where, like, they couldn't get it to stay and have the thing on top of it and still fire or whatever.

00:49:46.340 --> 00:49:48.500
We've talked about a lot in the game so far.

00:49:48.840 --> 00:49:55.820
And one big thing that I want to talk about, and big meaning I don't have much to say about it, but it kind of irked me.

00:49:55.820 --> 00:50:05.920
Is I still don't feel like the movement in Mega Man is as good as, you know, some of the other platformers that we praised on this show.

00:50:05.920 --> 00:50:07.120
And I don't know...

00:50:07.120 --> 00:50:10.280
I don't know what it is about it that's just not quite there.

00:50:10.580 --> 00:50:14.200
But it feels a little stiff being Mega Man.

00:50:14.220 --> 00:50:15.240
He's still a little sticky.

00:50:15.520 --> 00:50:20.880
His jump, unless you're underwater, feels like you should have, like, a few extra...

00:50:20.880 --> 00:50:24.800
A few extra pixels added onto the end of that.

00:50:26.720 --> 00:50:36.340
I mean, it's still, like, in the top 10% of movement mechanics I think we've seen in NES games.

00:50:36.360 --> 00:50:38.000
But you're right.

00:50:38.000 --> 00:50:40.380
It's not at the level of Super Mario.

00:50:40.700 --> 00:50:43.800
Yeah, and I'm not asking for him to be, like, floaty or anything.

00:50:43.800 --> 00:50:53.220
But even just, like, you know, sometimes there are platforms that, you know, require, like, you know, being very close to the edge to jump to land on the previous platform.

00:50:53.360 --> 00:50:55.780
And that's fine. Like, that's just something that NES games do.

00:50:56.020 --> 00:50:58.720
You know, a lot of games on the Essential Games list have that flaw as well.

00:50:58.980 --> 00:51:02.460
It's just that with Mega Man, you don't get, like, that...

00:51:02.460 --> 00:51:04.080
You don't get that running feel.

00:51:04.080 --> 00:51:06.680
You don't get that buildup, that momentum and everything.

00:51:06.740 --> 00:51:09.920
And I feel like maybe it's just throwing me off.

00:51:09.920 --> 00:51:12.440
But in games like Super Mario Bros.

00:51:12.620 --> 00:51:18.720
or Ninja Gaiden, you know, I just felt like I was more in control of my character.

00:51:18.920 --> 00:51:20.620
Whereas Mega Man is really powerful.

00:51:20.620 --> 00:51:26.640
So it feels easy to just, you know, stand your ground and fight off enemies and wait to move on, right?

00:51:26.740 --> 00:51:28.220
There's no rush to move on.

00:51:28.280 --> 00:51:31.320
Whereas in Super Mario Bros., you kind of always want to move forward.

00:51:31.320 --> 00:51:38.160
Because every time you stand there, you're either at risk of running the clock or getting hit, which is, you know, you only have two hits.

00:51:38.160 --> 00:51:40.340
In Mega Man, you got a pretty sizable health bar.

00:51:40.420 --> 00:51:42.620
You can always get it back. And you are strong.

00:51:42.700 --> 00:51:47.120
So I just feel like the movement is something that I can't quite put my finger on it.

00:51:47.220 --> 00:51:50.540
But I wish I was just more agile as Mega Man.

00:51:50.580 --> 00:51:56.760
I think it might have taken a bit away from, like, the actual shooting aspect of the game.

00:51:56.920 --> 00:52:02.280
Because if you're too agile, I think that that would make the entire game easier.

00:52:02.280 --> 00:52:15.420
And I think the balance of having the slightly crippled Mega Man boy that's got all the guns, I think that has, like, not a perfect balance.

00:52:15.420 --> 00:52:19.600
But it makes it feel like a Mega Man game and not Mario with guns.

00:52:21.100 --> 00:52:28.840
Yeah, I think that, like, what, for me, it feels like he doesn't have, like, the type of, like, weight that Mario has.

00:52:29.080 --> 00:52:36.540
Where he's got, like, momentum and he, you know, and he skids to a halt, which oddly makes it feel more, like, easily controllable.

00:52:38.720 --> 00:52:43.140
Whereas, like, for Mario, it feels like he's got this, like, weight that's combined with agility.

00:52:43.140 --> 00:52:44.720
Where he's, like, fluid and moving around.

00:52:44.820 --> 00:52:49.760
Where, like, Mega Man feels like, I guess, like, he's just got weight, you know?

00:52:49.900 --> 00:52:51.140
Like he's some kind of robot.

00:52:51.360 --> 00:52:53.960
So that's, yeah. So, like, that's maybe what they are going for.

00:52:54.160 --> 00:52:57.220
But, you know, I do feel like, yeah, the motion could be improved upon.

00:52:57.320 --> 00:53:04.160
But I also agree that I think if they did improve on the motion, they'd have to redesign the game slightly to, like, account for that.

00:53:04.160 --> 00:53:09.420
Because I do think it would make it a little too easy and maybe it would discourage you from using power-ups.

00:53:09.520 --> 00:53:13.240
Because there were even times, even with this motion, where I was like, okay, screw this.

00:53:13.300 --> 00:53:14.660
I'm just going to try and run past these people.

00:53:14.780 --> 00:53:15.980
And I did a couple times.

00:53:16.180 --> 00:53:24.760
And I feel like if I could, if I were playing as Mario in this game, you know, like, with that type of movement, I feel like I could blow by a lot of these enemies.

00:53:26.120 --> 00:53:27.840
Yeah. Yeah, that's an interesting thought.

00:53:27.840 --> 00:53:36.960
Because, like, any time that you're just struggling in a particular stage, provided that there's no, like, major pitfalls or platforming that you have to do,

00:53:36.980 --> 00:53:42.940
I feel like you have enough help that sometimes it's just worth it to take the initial knock, right?

00:53:42.940 --> 00:53:46.960
And then use your invincibility frames to just kind of get past everything.

00:53:46.960 --> 00:53:52.820
And that's not really a trick that we see often on these side-scrolling games.

00:53:52.940 --> 00:53:57.820
But because Mega Man is a, you know, it's moved in, like, a grid-like fashion, right?

00:53:57.900 --> 00:54:02.720
Yeah. You're in a square and then you move to another square, you know, like, Metroid style.

00:54:03.360 --> 00:54:06.640
I feel like you get away with that a little more.

00:54:06.640 --> 00:54:13.840
And it's only later in the game where they make that not so possible given the platforming perils.

00:54:14.080 --> 00:54:22.060
But through a lot of the, you know, like, introductory stages, you could just run right through a lot of things to just make sure that you have, you know,

00:54:22.120 --> 00:54:27.020
just enough health to get to the Robot Master and take him down if you have the appropriate power-up.

00:54:27.020 --> 00:54:31.700
Yeah, I remember at least one situation where I kept dying at a certain point.

00:54:32.800 --> 00:54:35.420
And, like, there was an enemy that kept hitting me.

00:54:35.420 --> 00:54:38.440
But then there were spikes.

00:54:38.440 --> 00:54:47.800
And I knew that if I touched a spike while I was invincible, it would just immediately take my life.

00:54:48.120 --> 00:54:53.640
But if I got hit by an enemy and then went into the spike, it wouldn't kill me.

00:54:53.640 --> 00:54:58.560
So I used that as a little bit of a workaround and just traded a little bit of life for a little bit of time.

00:55:00.600 --> 00:55:04.940
But, yeah, there's definitely strategy in taking damage.

00:55:05.800 --> 00:55:07.500
Wow, you're playing next level there.

00:55:07.620 --> 00:55:08.540
That's, like, real bad game.

00:55:08.540 --> 00:55:09.500
I was just lazy.

00:55:35.480 --> 00:55:39.740
Okay, we've done enough talking about, you know, like, first...

00:55:39.740 --> 00:55:41.480
No, just the first half of this game.

00:55:41.480 --> 00:55:42.320
Isn't that crazy?

00:55:42.480 --> 00:55:46.000
Like, we've been mostly talking about just the Robot Masters and that stuff.

00:55:46.000 --> 00:55:48.620
We've occasionally mentioned Wily Stage 4 for some reason.

00:55:48.740 --> 00:55:49.560
That one really irks us.

00:55:49.560 --> 00:55:54.400
But, like, there is a whole second half to this game after you beat all eight Robot Masters.

00:55:54.960 --> 00:55:58.300
Which is, you know, I'm not going to say that that's, like, hours of gameplay.

00:55:58.660 --> 00:56:01.440
But that's a pretty substantial, like, game in itself, right?

00:56:01.820 --> 00:56:08.860
Then you all of a sudden have to do, like, a, you know, a series of even more challenging platforming levels

00:56:08.860 --> 00:56:17.000
where the bosses are arguably much more challenging, only to be followed up with a boss rush of all the previous Robot Masters again.

00:56:17.160 --> 00:56:19.360
Just like they didn't learn their lesson from Mega Man 1.

00:56:19.420 --> 00:56:20.660
They were like, oh, let's do that again.

00:56:20.660 --> 00:56:21.460
That was exciting.

00:56:21.600 --> 00:56:24.120
Yeah. And then you actually have to fight Dr.

00:56:24.260 --> 00:56:29.500
Wily, don't forget. You would think in a normal game, and this, I think we talked about this in the first episode too.

00:56:29.700 --> 00:56:34.720
In a normal game, you would defeat the eight Robot Masters and then just be, like, summoned to a boss fight with Dr.

00:56:34.820 --> 00:56:36.980
Wily. Right? Like, that would just be the center screen.

00:56:37.160 --> 00:56:41.360
In this one, it's like, you have reached stage one of, what, six?

00:56:41.620 --> 00:56:42.760
Right? There's, like, six Dr.

00:56:42.800 --> 00:56:43.640
Wily stages. I think so, yeah.

00:56:43.700 --> 00:56:46.000
It's crazy. It's crazy that there's that many.

00:56:47.220 --> 00:56:50.800
I just, I want to get your opinion just on, like, the thought of that, right?

00:56:50.900 --> 00:56:56.300
That in a game where there is a password system and there's a lot going on to it,

00:56:56.920 --> 00:57:02.720
does, like, the game being divided between the eight Robot Masters and the six Wily Fortress stages,

00:57:02.720 --> 00:57:05.920
like, does that feel like a cohesive vision?

00:57:06.200 --> 00:57:13.500
Or does it feel like all of a sudden the difficulty and size of the game has just ramped up considerably?

00:57:14.140 --> 00:57:16.940
I think that it feels cohesive, honestly.

00:57:17.300 --> 00:57:24.420
I suspect we said something like this in the original game because it's the same thing in Mega Man 1, correct?

00:57:25.780 --> 00:57:28.040
Yeah, but I think there's only four stages.

00:57:28.040 --> 00:57:31.500
Right, okay, so it's a little, a little, so, like, they went a little further with it this time.

00:57:31.800 --> 00:57:36.620
But I, it gives you this kind of cool feeling where it's, like, especially with the password system,

00:57:36.820 --> 00:57:41.640
where it's, like, at first you're, you're just going through, you're just getting stronger,

00:57:41.640 --> 00:57:46.820
you're fighting all these, it's like you're preparing to go on your actual mission, you know?

00:57:46.820 --> 00:57:53.320
And then, like, once you've beaten all of these Robot Masters, you might be, like, you might,

00:57:53.320 --> 00:57:54.640
you might have taken some time to do that.

00:57:54.740 --> 00:57:56.940
You might have gotten, you know, especially if you're playing on difficult mode,

00:57:57.080 --> 00:57:59.380
you might have really been, like, learning and practicing.

00:57:59.580 --> 00:58:01.680
And now you, you have all these power-ups.

00:58:01.800 --> 00:58:06.160
You've, you've upgraded this robot to as upgraded as it can be.

00:58:06.920 --> 00:58:10.760
And now you're like, okay, now I'm ready to, like, go take on this mission.

00:58:10.880 --> 00:58:12.700
You know, it's like, it's like, that's all, like, the prep,

00:58:13.440 --> 00:58:15.020
which is a fun game in and of itself.

00:58:15.240 --> 00:58:17.440
And then you go on and it's not just a boss battle.

00:58:17.800 --> 00:58:23.200
It's this whole, like, progressing through this, I don't know, castle or fortress or whatever,

00:58:23.540 --> 00:58:28.300
fighting more bosses, you know, revisiting old bosses and then fighting the final battle.

00:58:28.380 --> 00:58:32.140
But it's like, it gives you the feeling like, well, if I had come here before

00:58:32.140 --> 00:58:34.880
when I didn't have all these power-ups, probably would have done a lot worse.

00:58:35.260 --> 00:58:37.660
So, like, that makes it feel like a satisfying progression.

00:58:38.080 --> 00:58:42.560
Yeah, I mean, I, I'm a fan of the structure of the game where, you know,

00:58:42.700 --> 00:58:47.040
beat these first eight and then, then you've got pretty much, like,

00:58:47.140 --> 00:58:50.360
the second half of the game that's a much more linear affair.

00:58:50.560 --> 00:58:52.520
Like, I think that's a cool structure.

00:58:52.520 --> 00:58:56.900
I guess my problem with, with it here is that there is,

00:58:57.040 --> 00:59:00.060
they don't really have as much fun with these levels,

00:59:01.080 --> 00:59:08.160
either aesthetically or design-wise than I think they were with the robot master stages.

00:59:09.680 --> 00:59:11.800
I don't know how you guys thought about that.

00:59:11.800 --> 00:59:13.260
Yeah, no, it's like, I get what you're saying.

00:59:13.420 --> 00:59:18.040
It's mostly just a dungeon, a cave, if you will, and it's very closed off.

00:59:18.360 --> 00:59:28.120
And a lot of it is, like, there's no sense of, you know, thematic entry to, like, the,

00:59:28.420 --> 00:59:34.600
I wasn't expecting to fight a big dragon at the end of Wily Stage 1, right?

00:59:34.740 --> 00:59:36.700
Like, it just, all of a sudden, it just kind of happens.

00:59:36.700 --> 00:59:41.120
It's like, oh, you got to, you got to his big lab, and then in the basement,

00:59:41.320 --> 00:59:43.440
there's a dragon with a bunch of floating platforms.

00:59:43.620 --> 00:59:44.580
It's like, sure, why not?

00:59:44.580 --> 00:59:45.940
Big pot-bellied dragon.

00:59:46.600 --> 00:59:48.240
Yeah, big pot-bellied dragon.

00:59:48.400 --> 00:59:53.020
Like, you know, I think that's just, I think that's the idea of, like, just being in a,

00:59:53.760 --> 00:59:55.020
in a dungeon, right?

00:59:55.020 --> 00:59:57.080
But it's just all very closed off.

00:59:57.240 --> 01:00:01.640
If you look at, like, the, the moment-to-moment gameplay in any of the Wily Fortress stages,

01:00:03.000 --> 01:00:08.140
a lot of it is like, oh, you really can't jump that high, or, oh, you really can only

01:00:09.760 --> 01:00:12.400
fall this certain way, because otherwise there's spikes.

01:00:13.500 --> 01:00:15.400
You know, there's a lot of pits and stuff like that.

01:00:15.500 --> 01:00:17.840
It's not very, it's not very welcoming.

01:00:18.160 --> 01:00:19.460
And I guess, why would Dr.

01:00:19.500 --> 01:00:21.080
Wily's Castle be said to be welcoming?

01:00:21.480 --> 01:00:23.900
But it's not as fun as a result of that, either.

01:00:24.320 --> 01:00:32.620
Yeah, it's very much based around just, like, skill testing, and not like, oh, this is a

01:00:32.620 --> 01:00:35.020
cool idea. It's like, no, avoid the spikes.

01:00:35.420 --> 01:00:37.080
Yeah, I can see that, too.

01:00:37.160 --> 01:00:40.400
I mean, I guess they were probably trying to, like, make it be like, okay, now it's all about,

01:00:40.480 --> 01:00:44.500
yeah, now it's all about what you've learned, and it's not about, I don't know, yeah.

01:00:44.580 --> 01:00:49.580
It does feel like it, it's straight away from that, like, really interesting level design,

01:00:49.580 --> 01:00:52.680
and it just kind of went for, like, okay, now it's just, now it's just difficult.

01:00:53.620 --> 01:00:56.400
Which isn't the end of the world, but yeah, it would have been nice to have some, like,

01:00:56.620 --> 01:00:59.760
some, some new interesting curveballs to be thrown in there.

01:00:59.920 --> 01:01:08.520
But I will be damned if, you know, the Mecha Dragon, or whatever he's called, and the Bulldozer

01:01:08.520 --> 01:01:15.120
guy, if those two aren't, like, so much cooler than the Yellow Devil, and also more fun to

01:01:15.120 --> 01:01:16.860
fight than the Yellow Devil.

01:01:17.520 --> 01:01:20.700
I get it, the Yellow Devil has a pattern, if you figure it out, it's easy.

01:01:21.080 --> 01:01:24.520
Trust me, I've watched videos on it, I still can't do it, so I'm just bad at video games.

01:01:25.500 --> 01:01:30.820
The Yellow Devil was the guy, yeah, first game, he appears, he's got like a bit, you

01:01:30.820 --> 01:01:35.220
know, he's like a cyclops, and then his body morphs over to the other side of the stage.

01:01:35.220 --> 01:01:37.580
Cuts up into chunks. Oh, right, yeah, it was awful.

01:01:37.700 --> 01:01:39.180
You have to dodge the blocks, it's awful.

01:01:39.180 --> 01:01:45.260
That's right, yeah. Yeah, whereas Mecha Dragon, it's like, yeah, you can only take damage in the head or whatever,

01:01:45.280 --> 01:01:49.340
and if he hits you, you could fall off the platforms and stuff like that, but as long

01:01:49.340 --> 01:01:52.100
as you're on the top platform, I feel like you're gonna fall onto the other platforms,

01:01:52.160 --> 01:01:53.400
so it's just a matter of coming back up to the top.

01:01:53.400 --> 01:01:56.060
It's not as much of a frustration battle.

01:01:57.020 --> 01:02:00.720
Yeah, yeah, it's like, I don't know, it's just like, they look better, right?

01:02:01.400 --> 01:02:05.560
All of a sudden, like, the sprite quality, you could fool me with that Bulldozer guy, like,

01:02:05.580 --> 01:02:07.400
I would think that's a Super Nintendo graphic.

01:02:08.300 --> 01:02:09.540
Yeah, it is.

01:02:09.540 --> 01:02:18.000
Yeah, really. It's very much, very much in the, keeping with the design that sort of went along, that this

01:02:18.000 --> 01:02:23.180
game went for going forward several decades, it's kind of timeless.

01:02:23.600 --> 01:02:31.600
Yeah, and I just, like, overall, I think the boss fights in Wily Fortress are great, with

01:02:31.600 --> 01:02:36.000
the exception of the one where you have to strategically use your crash bombers that you don't run out,

01:02:36.000 --> 01:02:40.520
only because, and here's my problem with that, Joe, before you tell me why it's good.

01:02:40.960 --> 01:02:47.900
The problem is, is that there's no, like, way to get more of that, so if you screw up, right,

01:02:48.020 --> 01:02:50.560
it's like, it's just, it's just over, right?

01:02:50.660 --> 01:02:54.500
Like, you have to wait till the turrets kill you, and then you have to start that stage over,

01:02:54.640 --> 01:02:58.300
and I just feel like there's gotta be a better way to handle this.

01:02:58.380 --> 01:03:02.940
Like, you have so many other power-ups, and the only thing that can take them down is the crash bomber.

01:03:02.940 --> 01:03:04.780
It should have been a loophole.

01:03:04.900 --> 01:03:06.620
Yeah, I mean, I completely agree with that, too.

01:03:06.760 --> 01:03:11.460
That, and there's another instance in the final boss battle, where, yeah, it's the same thing,

01:03:11.540 --> 01:03:15.840
where I feel like, without any warning that this is what you're going to need for this battle,

01:03:16.660 --> 01:03:20.780
it doesn't feel good to get there, realize you just don't have enough ammo to beat it,

01:03:20.820 --> 01:03:23.580
and there's no way of getting ammo, and then having to start the level over,

01:03:23.720 --> 01:03:24.940
and remember to keep the ammo.

01:03:25.040 --> 01:03:28.340
Like, you should have some warning, just so it's not just, like, get there,

01:03:28.340 --> 01:03:34.460
and then realize that that's actually some of the same type of problem that we had in the first game,

01:03:34.560 --> 01:03:38.440
where it's like you get to the point, realize you needed something earlier,

01:03:38.440 --> 01:03:41.440
and have no choice but to die and go back to earlier.

01:03:41.680 --> 01:03:46.700
Where it's like, well, yeah, it just feels like a waste of time.

01:03:47.340 --> 01:03:51.620
I think that the easiest way that they could have solved this was, like, I don't know,

01:03:51.740 --> 01:03:57.720
have some easy mob also moving around the stage that you could kill,

01:03:57.740 --> 01:04:02.880
and, I don't know, half the time it would drop some of the ammo,

01:04:04.060 --> 01:04:06.600
instead of you just sort of being alone with the turrets.

01:04:06.680 --> 01:04:10.580
Like, yeah, it makes the boss a little bit harder,

01:04:10.580 --> 01:04:16.820
because then you also have to deal with, like, just keeping an eye on these other little mobs running around,

01:04:16.840 --> 01:04:18.700
but at least it's beatable.

01:04:19.640 --> 01:04:20.620
Right, exactly.

01:04:21.160 --> 01:04:23.360
Yeah, and Joe, you talking about, you know,

01:04:23.500 --> 01:04:25.660
if we just want to jump straight to the end here for a second,

